    {
      "id": "95h88gb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Carbohydrates"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zg16gea",
      "content": "• Carbohydrates are the main source of energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cu0b3zv",
      "content": "• They are broken down into glucose."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j105pr6",
      "content": "• Stored in the liver and muscles as glycogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "A balanced diet contains all essential nutrients in the correct proportions required for growth, repair, and maintenance of health.",
      "id": "m0guabu"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f1nyac",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Proteins"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s0ab4y6",
      "content": "• Proteins are essential for growth and repair of tissues."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f48pg9x",
      "content": "• They are composed of amino acids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p1iuems",
      "content": "• Important for enzymes and hormones."
    },
    {
      "id": "26wppkk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Fats"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "djqaavu",
      "content": "• Fats provide twice as much energy as carbohydrates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zciz06f",
      "content": "• They help in absorption of vitamins A, D, E and K."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dr1l0kf",
      "content": "• They protect internal organs."
    },
